// Title: Turla Group Lateral Movement
// Sigma ID: c601f20d-570a-4cde-a7d6-e17f99cb8e7f
// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Markus Neis
// Date: 2017-11-07 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: G0010, execution, T1059, lateral-movement, T1021.002, discovery, T1083, T1135
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects automated lateral movement by Turla group
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://securelist.com/the-epic-turla-operation/65545/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules-emerging-threats/2014/TA/Turla/proc_creation_win_apt_turla_commands_critical.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine startswith "net use \\\\%DomainController%\\C$ \"P@ssw0rd\" " or (ProcessCommandLine contains "dir c:\\" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".doc" and ProcessCommandLine contains " /s") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "dir %TEMP%\\" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".exe")
